      "title": "Optimized Assets: next/image and next/font",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Optimized Assets: next/image and next/font",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. next/image Basics",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`<Image>` ==resizes==, converts to **WebP/AVIF**, lazy-loads",
                "Reserves space, so no layout shift (==CLS==)",
                "Needs `src` + `width` + `height`, or `fill` in a `position: relative` parent",
                "Static import gives width, height, `blurDataURL` free"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Loading and Remote Hosts",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Image",
                "Use"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Above-fold LCP",
                  "`priority` (preload)"
                ],
                [
                  "Everything else",
                  "lazy by default"
                ],
                [
                  "Responsive or `fill`",
                  "`sizes` avoids viewport-wide file"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "images: {",
                "  remotePatterns: [{",
                "    protocol: 'https',",
                "    hostname: 'cdn.example.com',",
                "    pathname: '/img/**',",
                "  }],",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "in next.config; unlisted host errors at request time"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. next/font",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "import { Inter } from 'next/font/google'",
                "const inter = Inter({ display: 'swap' })",
                "// <body className={inter.className}>"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Sources: `next/font/google` or `next/font/local`",
                "==Build-time== download, **self-hosted**, no Google requests",
                "Apply `className` or `variable` on `<html>`/`<body>`",
                "**When must LCP get priority?** Always for the hero image",
                "**Why remotePatterns?** Blocks unknown hosts"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Metadata API and SEO",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Metadata API and SEO",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Defining Metadata",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Export static ==metadata== or async ==generateMetadata({ params })==",
                "Only in `layout.tsx` or `page.tsx`, **Server Components** only",
                "Child segments **override and merge** with parent metadata"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Field",
                "Value"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`title`",
                  "string or `{ template: '%s | Site', default }`"
                ],
                [
                  "`description`",
                  "plain string"
                ],
                [
                  "`openGraph`, `twitter`",
                  "share card data"
                ],
                [
                  "`alternates.canonical`",
                  "canonical URL"
                ],
                [
                  "`robots`",
                  "index / follow rules"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`generateMetadata` fetches data for dynamic pages",
                "Same `fetch` as the page is ==deduplicated==: no double request"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Files and JSON-LD",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "File",
                "Served as"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`app/sitemap.ts`",
                  "`/sitemap.xml`"
                ],
                [
                  "`app/robots.ts`",
                  "`/robots.txt`"
                ],
                [
                  "`opengraph-image.tsx`",
                  "OG image"
                ],
                [
                  "`icon.png`, `favicon.ico`",
                  "site icons"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "JSON-LD is not metadata",
              "text": "Render a `<script type='application/ld+json'>` tag inside the **page component**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Environment Variables and Bundle Analysis",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Environment Variables and Bundle Analysis",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Load order and files",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "process.env",
                    "sub": "wins",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".env.local",
                    "sub": "not in test",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".env.development / .production",
                    "sub": ".env.test",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".env",
                    "sub": "defaults",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==.env.local== holds secrets: keep it out of **git**",
                "Real `process.env` beats every file"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Client vs server",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Name",
                "Where it lives",
                "In browser"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`NEXT_PUBLIC_API`",
                  "inlined at **build**",
                  "{green:value}"
                ],
                [
                  "`DB_URL`",
                  "server only",
                  "{red:undefined}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Frozen at build",
              "text": "`NEXT_PUBLIC_` values change only with a ==rebuild==. For runtime values, read server-only vars in a **dynamic route**."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Bundle analysis and fixes",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "js",
              "lines": [
                "// npm i @next/bundle-analyzer",
                "const withBundleAnalyzer = require('@next/bundle-analyzer')({",
                "  enabled: process.env.ANALYZE === 'true',",
                "})",
                "module.exports = withBundleAnalyzer(nextConfig)"
              ],
              "note": "wrap next.config"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Run `ANALYZE=true next build`: treemap reports open",
                "Check the ==First Load JS== column in build output"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`next/dynamic` or `React.lazy` for heavy client components",
                "Import only the needed functions from libraries",
                "Move work to **Server Components**: ships no JS"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Output Modes: Default, Standalone and Static Export",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Output Modes: Default, Standalone and Static Export",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Default and Standalone",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{green:Default}: `next build` then `next start` runs a ==Node server==",
                "Supports SSR, ISR, route handlers, middleware, image optimization",
                "`output: 'standalone'` traces needed files into ==.next/standalone==",
                "Gets a minimal `server.js` and trimmed `node_modules`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "# next.config: output: 'standalone'",
                "cp -r public .next/standalone/public",
                "cp -r .next/static .next/standalone/.next/static",
                "node .next/standalone/server.js"
              ],
              "note": "copy the assets, then run"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Standalone skips assets",
              "text": "It does not copy `public/` or `.next/static`. Copy them in, or serve from a CDN, or assets return ==404==."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Static Export",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`output: 'export'` emits plain HTML/CSS/JS to ==out/==",
                "No server: host on any static host or CDN",
                "Dynamic routes need `generateStaticParams`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "No SSR or request-time rendering",
                "No route handlers that read the request",
                "No middleware, no ISR",
                "Default image loader fails: `unoptimized: true` or a custom loader"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Side by Side",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Default",
                "standalone",
                "export"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Run",
                  "`next start`",
                  "`node server.js`",
                  "static host"
                ],
                [
                  "Server",
                  "Node",
                  "Node, minimal",
                  "{red:none}"
                ],
                [
                  "SSR / ISR",
                  "{green:yes}",
                  "{green:yes}",
                  "{red:no}"
                ],
                [
                  "Output",
                  "`.next`",
                  "`.next/standalone`",
                  "`out/`"
                ]
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Deploying to Vercel or a Node Server",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Deploying to Vercel or a Node Server",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Vercel",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Connect the Git repo: ==every push builds== automatically",
                "{blue:Preview} per branch/PR, {green:Production} on the main branch",
                "Env vars set per environment: Production, Preview, Development",
                "Routes → serverless/edge functions, static → CDN, ISR and images managed with ==zero config=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Self-Hosted Node and Docker",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "next build",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "next start -p 3000",
                    "sub": "or node .next/standalone/server.js",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "PM2 / systemd",
                    "sub": "supervise",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "nginx / LB",
                    "sub": "TLS + gzip",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Docker multi-stage: ==deps → build → runner== using the standalone output"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "dockerfile",
              "lines": [
                "FROM node:22-alpine AS runner",
                "USER nextjs",
                "ENV PORT=3000 HOSTNAME=0.0.0.0",
                "EXPOSE 3000",
                "CMD [\"node\", \"server.js\"]"
              ],
              "note": "non-root user, bind to all interfaces"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Self-Hosting Tradeoffs",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "You own",
                "Do"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Image optimization cache",
                  "install `sharp`"
                ],
                [
                  "ISR/data cache",
                  "custom cache handler across instances"
                ],
                [
                  "`/_next/static`",
                  "cache it on a CDN"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Build-time env",
              "text": "Build-time env must be present during `next build`."
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Interview Point: why a custom cache handler?** Multiple instances don't share the ISR cache by default",
                "**Vercel vs Node?** Vercel manages functions, CDN and ISR; on Node you run all of it"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "purple"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Production Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Production Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Image and Font",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Must know"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`next/image`",
                  "`width`+`height` or `fill`; `priority` for LCP; `sizes` if responsive; `remotePatterns` for remote hosts"
                ],
                [
                  "`next/font`",
                  "`google` or `local`; ==build-time==, self-hosted; `className` on `<body>`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Metadata and SEO",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Export `metadata` or async `generateMetadata`",
                "`title.template` sets the title pattern, e.g. `%s | Site`",
                "`app/sitemap.ts` and `app/robots.ts` are served automatically",
                "JSON-LD: a `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">` tag in the page"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Env and Analysis",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`NEXT_PUBLIC_` is ==build-time== and client-visible",
                "`ANALYZE=true next build` with `@next/bundle-analyzer`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Output and Deploy",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Mode",
                "Run",
                "Note"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "default",
                  "`next start`",
                  "Node server"
                ],
                [
                  "`standalone`",
                  "`node server.js`",
                  "copy `public` and `.next/static`"
                ],
                [
                  "`export`",
                  "`out/`",
                  "static only"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{green:Vercel}: push to deploy",
                "{blue:Node}: PM2 or Docker behind a proxy"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Standalone skips `public` and `.next/static`: copy them or assets return **404**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "You add `<Image src=\"https://cdn.shop.com/a.jpg\" width={400} height={300} alt=\"\" />` and it throws at request time. What's missing?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "The host isn't allow-listed in `remotePatterns` in next.config.",
                "Add protocol, hostname and pathname for cdn.shop.com."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "You set `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` in the host dashboard and restart the running server. The browser still calls the old URL. Why?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "`NEXT_PUBLIC_` values are inlined into the client bundle at build time.",
                "Only a rebuild picks up the new value."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Your standalone Docker container runs `node server.js`, but CSS, JS and images return 404. Fix?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Standalone doesn't copy `public/` or `.next/static`.",
                "Copy both into the standalone folder, or serve them from a CDN."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
